#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Moves two beads opened in a cloud session onto the Dolt remote, keeping their IDs
# (projectorange-browser-td5, projectorange-browser-kvq — commit 303a0a6 refers to them).
# The cloud session could not push refs/dolt/data itself (403: its git access is scoped to its branch).
# Run from your ProjectOrange-Browser checkout. Safe to re-run: import upserts by ID.
set -euo pipefail
bd dolt pull
bd import - <<'BEADS_JSONL'
{"_type":"issue","id":"projectorange-browser-td5","title":"Visual fidelity pass: lighting, shadows, shaders, particles (not ship models)","description":"Raise overall visual fidelity without touching ship geometry. Scope: scene lighting (key/fill/rim balance, environment reflections, light colour/falloff), shadows (ships and props casting onto the arena, sensible shadow budget), shaders (hull/arena surface response, emissive/bloom balance, post-processing), particles (engine trails, explosions, sparks, smoke, hit impacts, pickups). Constraints: keep the existing graphics-quality settings meaningful (low tier must stay cheap), no gameplay or netcode changes, keep the orange hue band reserved for oranges/power feedback (design doc). Verify with before/after screenshots via the repro harness and typecheck + tests green. Ship model geometry is split out to its own bead.","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Claude","owner":"noreply@anthropic.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T08:35:51Z","created_by":"Claude","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:37:20Z","started_at":"2026-11-08T08:35:54Z","lease_expires_at":"2026-11-08T08:40:54Z","heartbeat_at":"2026-11-08T08:35:54Z","comments":[{"id":"26190db0-6e5e-5713-8da7-21059a1017e1","issue_id":"projectorange-browser-td5","author":"Claude","text":"Progress: High tier gets n8ao SSAO (half-res, radius 10 m) + one shadow-casting light (nearest room light, ships-only casters, 1024 cube, fade-in on reassignment; moon + arena casters on outdoor maps). All tiers but Low: grade (sat +0.12, contrast +0.08, vignette), ambient dust. All tiers: plasma fireball shader for deaths/missiles (staggered secondary bursts), white-hot sparks with gravity, hot glowing debris with smoke trails, noise smoke with top light + blast glow, exhaust plume shader. Shadows/AO kept off Default per design doc §0.2 (60 FPS on 2019 iGPU). Cloak shimmer casts no shadow.","created_at":"2026-11-08T09:05:08Z"},{"id":"9778b840-2d36-53be-ad46-9d4614a755c5","issue_id":"projectorange-browser-td5","author":"Claude","text":"Pushed 303a0a6 on ccr-282871ad-rntce3. Verified in headless Chromium (SwiftShader): same-frame off/on on all 4 maps; shadow pipeline confirmed with a test plane; frame centre within 1-4% of old brightness after retune; practice-smoke (Low) and a Default-tier run clean; typecheck + 152 tests green. Bundle +88 KB gzip (n8ao). Not yet done: frame-time check of High tier (AO + shadows) on a real GPU — software GL can't measure it.","created_at":"2026-11-08T09:18:28Z"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":2}
{"_type":"issue","id":"projectorange-browser-kvq","title":"Ship model geometry pass: ship models read as too basic","description":"The four procedural ship models (Dart, Mule, Scythe, Brute in packages/client/src/ships/models.ts) look primitive: raw boxes/cylinders, little surface break-up, plain nozzles. Raise fidelity within design-doc §7.8 gates (\u003c=6k tris, \u003c=6 draw calls per ship after mergeByMaterial, silhouettes distinguishable) without changing shared hull sections, colliders, hit volumes or muzzle/engine anchors. Split out of projectorange-browser-td5, which covers lighting/shadows/shaders/particles first.","status":"open","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"noreply@anthropic.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T08:37:20Z","created_by":"Claude","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:37:20Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
